# MOST IMPORTANT CHEAT SHEET

```text
ASYMMETRIC
Public Key  → Share
Private Key → Secret
```

```text
ENCRYPTION
Public Key  → Encrypt
Private Key → Decrypt
```

```text
DIGITAL SIGNATURE
Private Key → Sign
Public Key  → Verify
```

```text
SSH
known_hosts     → Known server keys
authorized_keys → Allowed client public keys
```

```text
HTTPS
TLS Certificate → Web server identity
CA              → Certificate trust
```

```text
GPG
gpg --full-gen-key
        ↓
Generate GPG key

gpg --import backup.key
        ↓
Import key

gpg --decrypt message.gpg
        ↓
Decrypt GPG message
```

## One-line Memory Trick

**"Public key to lock/encrypt, private key to unlock/decrypt; private key to sign, public key to verify."**

And remember:

**A web server uses a TLS certificate to prove its identity to the client.**
